# Fetched data and the generated site are both rebuilt fresh by
# update_all.py every run (locally or in CI) -- committing them would just
# bloat the repo's history with constantly regenerated JSON/HTML for no
# benefit. Nothing here is a source file.
belt_data/
site/

# historical_data/ is DELIBERATELY NOT ignored -- it's the small, git-
# committed baseline (settled reigns/belt games + settled box scores) that
# lets build_lineage.py and fetch_game_details.py fetch only the current +
# previous season each run instead of CFBD's whole history every time. See
# README.md's "Incremental fetching" section.
#
# ai_preview_cache/ is also DELIBERATELY NOT ignored, same idea -- it's the
# last AI-generated upcoming-game preview, keyed to exactly which game it's
# for, so generate_ai_preview.py only spends a real Claude API call when
# the upcoming game actually changes instead of on every run.

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
